stefan

1st of all: ***why*** transtec ??? 
its *much* to expensive imho.

signal 11 indicates a hardware problem.

my alpha worked like a charm until the day i installed the new 128mb
memory (4*32mb bus still at 128bit). 

i bought the new memory from:

       TRANSTEC 

( i dont like them, but it seemed hard to get true parity nowadays).

this worked fine for the first few days. 

Then i did recompile XF86 3.3 and had the first 'gcc signal 11 errors'
The box crashed sometimes without any reason. 

It also crashed under NT4.0 with "irq not less or equal' or 'memory bus
error' (iam not shure but i think that was what NT said (its hard to
remember those funny messages)).

So send them the RAM back, and they replaced it without trouble.
I never experienced similar problems again.

best regards,
--armin


 ---------------------------------------------------------------------
