>but scsiinfo reports that the bad block list isn't growing and I'm
>not hearing any type of nasty sounds after startup.
Most of the SCSI drives may not start until they receive a start command.
Depends on jumper settings. MAybe the HD spinning up.
As you mentioned, the Barracuda and Cheetah drives from Seagate are noisy
and hot little animals. I prefer Quantum or Fujitsu.



