> 
> When I try to execute a byte code file which I compiled on an NT (yeah,
> thanks to Bill I can compile java programs...) machine using kaffe I get an
> error stating that kaffe cannot find the native libraries in path...
.....
> ./lib/libnative.so.0.92
> ./lib/libnative.so
> ./lib/libnet.so.0.92
> ./lib/libnet.so
> ./lib/libagent.so.0.92
> ./lib/libagent.so
> ./lib/libzip.so.0.92
> ./lib/libzip.so
> ./lib/libkaffevm.so.0.92
> ./lib/libkaffevm.so
> ./lib/classes.zip

These are shared libraries.  Did you rerun ldconfig after you put
all these libraries there?  If some of that went into /usr/local/lib
you have to make sure that this path is included in /etc/ld.so.conf
before that run.

ldconfig runs every time from a startup scripts when you boot but if
you installed new shared libraries somewhere you have make sure that
re-running ldconfig is a part of a startup process.


  Michal


