>same "call" conventions? ( linux, freebsd, caldera, Yggdrasil, and so on )
>hum....

No they aren't.  They typically differ from OS to OS.  However, for
the class of OS's called 'Linux', they are all really close.  Linux/Alpha
supports Digital's 'COFF' format as well as ELF; I imagine that Linux/SPARC
supports Sun's a.out.  The calling convention for a particular Linux/architecture
is probably (but not required) to be the same for all distributions for
that architecture.

I hope this helps.

