that's something I didn't notice (and I would call that a bug rather
than a feature). But fillbytes() and movebytes() are now 64bit clean.

> The other problem is that cdrecord does not want to run on Alpha with
> a default fifo size of 4 Megs.  I did not have a time to track down

You must increase the maximum allowed shm segment size in your kernel.
To do this you have to change SHMMAX. Mine looks like this:

#define SHMMAX 0x2000000                /* max shared seg size (bytes) */

Just for the record, since cdrecord-1.6a11 my JVC writer is able to burn
CDs on my Alpha machine. Older versions of cdrecord the fixiating stage
didn't terminate.

