On Wed, 25 Mar 1998, "Jochen K\"upper" wrote:
>Well, I compiled kernel 2.0.33 with the axp patch applied. I configured =
it=0D
>to support Alpha a.out binaries.=0D
>=0D
>Whenever I try to run a Digital Unix binary - like netscape for DU 3.2,=0D
>it says:=0D
>> /usr/local/share/netscape/netscape=0D
>bash: /usr/local/share/netscape/netscape: No such file or directory=0D
>=0D
>The file exists for sure, it does have the right permissions, the binary=
=0D
>does work on DU, ...=0D
>=0D
>Any hint/help ?=0D
>Jochen=0D

"No such file or directory" in this case usually means that the program c=
an't
find one or more of the libraries that it needs. Try ldd netscape and see=
 what
happens (although I'm not sure ldd would work with a DU binary).

Do you have the required DU libs installed? You need:

LinXm.so
linXmu.so
libm.so
libX11.so
libXt.so
libdnet.so
libc.so
linXext.so

All installed in /usr/shlib.

You also need /sbin/loader

All this assumes you are running the DU 3.2 libs. Things get uglier if oy=
u're
trying to use the 4.0x libs.

Check the FAQ at azstarnet for more info.


--
Brian E.W. Wood  beww@intac.com

