On Wed, 25 Mar 1998 Jay.Estabrook@digital.com wrote:

> >>> fade@wookiee.deepsky.com said:
> >
> > I was shocked when I viewed Digital's Titanic promotional site at
> > http://www.digital.com/gigahit/  ...  not by the obvious quality of the
> > site, but by the specific omition of any mention of Linux in the vaunted
> > renderfarm that they're evangelizing. Moreover, the specific mention of
> > DigitalUNIX within the framework of that site is misleading in that it
> > implies that it was the OS used in the production. Opinions?
> 
> A more "impartial" review, shall we say, may be had from the Digital
> Semiconductor webpage at:
> 
> 	http://www.digital.com/semiconductor/alpha/alpha-21264anncmt.htm
> 
> This page contains links to the Carrera page and the LJ article.
> 
> --Jay++

Well, I managed to start quite the little thread. Perhaps my reaction was
a bit naive, but I'm a fan of the underdog, especially when the underdog
is such a promising platform. It's dissappointing to me that a company
like Digital doesn't trumpet the things it's doing to support the free
software model; giving direct support to the Linux comunity by hardware
donations and providing engineering talent to things like bootstrap code
etc. is an incredible thing and full of potential for beneficient media
coverage - especially when the product was something as huge as this
movie. It's in the consciousness of the popular culture, which is a rare
and valuable opportunity. The use of an upstart operating system licensed
for free distribution to the whole world in such a mamoth undertaking is a
coup of unforseen proportions. Instead DEC's "spin-doctors" (to use your
phrasing) decided to promote Microsoft's NT "operating system". I
understand the promotion of Digital products on a digital site, but if
you're going to (I'm being euphamistic when I say "you") promote third
party issues, then why not present that truthfully, and evenly.. is
digital embarassed about its associations with the Linux community that
has embraced it's hardware and put it to such good use?

I don't mean to be a zealot; it's just that I'm typing this on an NT box
that has crashed on me four times in the past five hours, and it forces me
to think that my Alpha Linux box has been up for eighty days... p'raps
we'll just mark that up with the things that make you go "Hmmmm"...

Brian
fade@etc.etc.etc.

"It is error alone which needs the support of government. Truth can
stand by itself." -- Thomas Jefferson


