James D. Freels wrote:
> >
> >Is it possible to install Windows NT, Linux and Digital
> >Unix on one hard disk? Which loader should I use?
> 
> Yes, I have one I purchased turn-key from Microway.

On one disk, or on one machine?  This is not the same thing.
AFAIK NT knows only about "FAT style" partition tables for disks,
Digital Unix uses only "BSD type" disk labels (where partitions
can, and do, overlap).  Linux on Alpha understands both schemes.
So it is possible to have two disks for three OSes but one disk
seem to be hard; or there is some trick to overlap both tables?
(sounds very iffy).

A loader situation will be "interesting". :-)  You will have to 
juggle between SRM and ARC/AlphaBIOS.

> The trick is getting compatible
> peripherals that will work with the 3 OSs, DEC-Unix being the most
> difficult. 

The current 4.0D version of DU seem to be much more accomodating -
especially with graphics cards.

  Michal
  


