> How would I go about adding support for a serial console into the kernel?
> SRM and MILO see the terminal (9600 bps, 8N1) on COM1, but when I boot
the
> kernel, I lose interactivity. The host is a PC164LX. TIA,
Yep, had the same problem not long ago on an alphastation200, but I suppose
it
would be the same for any linux system.

try adding the following entry to your /etc/inittab:

con1:2345:respawn:/sbin/getty ttyS0 console vt100
con2:2345:respawn:/sbin/getty ttyS1 console vt100

Oh, and recompile your kernel to add serial support ! It asks two things
about serial:
something about modems (decide wether you need it or not...) and something
else
that is what you're looking for (can't remember the exact wording ).

