On Wed, Mar 25, 1998 at 10:30:45AM +0100, Ralph Gillen wrote:
> So, I recompiled my kernel (2.0.30, RH5.0) with this change, compiled 
> cdrecord-1.6a11 (and cdrecord-1.6a12), and everything I get from cdrecord is a 
> crash when calling it.
> 
> Please, could somebody (Thomas?) help me and give me some more information on 
> which kernel, libc etc. version you use? I´m fighting with this for two weeks 
> now and I really don´t like the idea to put my CDR into a PC 8-(

you have three options to solve your problem:-)

1. Upgrade to a newer kernel 2.0.32 or 2.0.33 will do the trick.

2. Uncomment the mprotect() call in cdrecord

3. Use the patch below (taken from patch-2.0.31).

I also had to upgrade the NCR driver, because my JVC CDR didn't work with
version 1.12 (included in < 2.0.31). 

Thomas.

diff -u --recursive --new-file v2.0.30/linux/mm/mlock.c linux/mm/mlock.c
--- v2.0.30/linux/mm/mlock.c    Wed Sep 11 07:57:19 1996
+++ linux/mm/mlock.c    Wed Oct 15 15:58:46 1997
@@ -124,9 +124,9 @@
                        pages = -pages;
                vma->vm_mm->locked_vm += pages;
 
-               if (newflags & VM_LOCKED)
+               if ((newflags & VM_LOCKED) && (newflags & VM_READ))
                        while (start < end) {
-                               char c = get_user((char *) start);
+                               int c = get_user((int *) start);
                                __asm__ __volatile__("": :"r" (c));
                                start += PAGE_SIZE;
                        }




