> alone Alphas!

Here's my two cents:

1. the Bus Logic may be a fine card (I've no personal experience, but have
   heard a *lot* of good reports), BUT it has one drawback: you won't be able
   to set up the system to boot MILO from any disk on it. This is because
   the ARC/AlphaBIOS/SRM consoles don't have drivers for it. You could, of
   course, boot MILO off one of the builtin NCR810's disks, and then a kernel,
   etc, from the BusLogic...

2. I have had "close encounters of the weird kind" with Adaptecs, recently,
   mostly during configuration/bus probing, which I've had to find work-
   arounds for. However, once the system is configured cleanly, they do
   seem to work reasonably, and they are supported by ARC/AlphaBIOS, but
   *not* SRM, which, with an XL366, is not an option, anyway... ;-}

3. There's a number of NCR875-based boards (Symbios, Intraserver, etc) that
   work quite nicely, and are supported by all the consoles and LINUX.

Good luck with your choice...

--Jay++

