Autodetecting disks with fdisk: the trick.

Fdisk on the alpha shows some slightly strange behavior where it will not
autodetect the disks _however_ it is possible to detect disks by using the
following 'hack':

1) fire up fdisk on the drive. Set it to obnoxiously high disk
paramaters.. I like 63 sectors, 64 heads, 9999 cyls. Then create one
partition, and <W>rite it to disk. run fdisk again, and delete the
partition you created. You will find fdisk now knows the disk geometry.
Create your partitions normally, and go. 

This only works on SCSI devices, I think.

S.


