Thanks.  That's one brute force approach.
The diff between these two directories is 5.8 Mbytes.
As for 1.0.2, egcs-1.0.2 can't handle negative array bounds
combined with an asteric for the upper bound. 
The latest snap can, but it can't do a "write"....
Try this:

      program bomb
      integer iname(-1:3)
      iname(2) = 2
      call pow(iname)
      stop
      end

      subroutine pow(iname)
      integer iname(-1:*)
        Write(6,1000) iname(2)
 1000   Format(' iname(2) = ',i5)
      return
      end

